---
/**
 * Port of casestudy/run.html. The only case study using CaseStudyLayout's
 * named "hero" slot instead of `heroImage`: source's hero is a YouTube
 * `<iframe>`, not a background image. `class="hero"` goes on the wrapping
 * div (matching source structure) so HeroImage's `:global(.hero)` rule
 * gives it `height: 100%`. `loading="lazy"` added per the plan's explicit
 * "slots for ... run.html YouTube iframe (lazy)" note.
 *
 * Sizing (a11y fix, 2026-07-30): source's `width="100%" height="100%"` on
 * the iframe are dropped and replaced with scoped CSS (`width/height: 100%`
 * on the iframe, filling HeroImage's fixed-height box) —
 * same "no attribute sizing on embeds" rule `ContentMedia` already
 * enforces, and it means the box is reserved before the iframe (or its CSS)
 * finishes loading, so nothing shifts.
 */
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import ContentBlock from '../../components/ContentBlock.astro';
import ContentMedia from '../../components/ContentMedia.astro';
import Divider from '../../components/Divider.astro';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Yandex.Run — running music case study · Jury Alyavdin"
  description="How Yandex.Run matched music tempo to a runner's pace, built during Yandex's School of Mobile Design."
  path="/casestudy/run.html"
  h1="Music that fits with the pace of the runner"
  avatarImage="/casestudy/run/run.png"
  orbitTop="Yandex.Run"
  orbitBottom="Music Streaming"
  glow="#080808"
  details={[
    { label: 'Platform', value: 'Android' },
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Product Designer' },
    { label: 'Date', value: '2016' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="hero" slot="hero">
    <iframe
      src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/3_RzI-oWqK4"
      title="YouTube video player"
      loading="lazy"
      frameborder="0"
      allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
      allowfullscreen
    ></iframe>
  </div>

  <ContentBlock title="Overview">
    <p>
      The School of Mobile Design was held at Yandex. Participants were expected to be immersed in the specifics
      of creating mobile products from an idea and its verification to the launch of a finished application. The
      participants who successfully completed the first stage moved on to the second, where they had to carry out
      a joint project with managers and developers.
    </p>
  </ContentBlock>

  <ContentBlock title="Goal">
    <p>
      The main goal was to find a product-market fit of the new cross-service based on the radio streaming
      technology from Yandex.Music service.
    </p>
    <Divider />
  </ContentBlock>

  <ContentBlock title="Solution">
    <p>
      As a product team, we came with a solution to mix radio streaming technology with the user's pace at
      running. It helped us find a solution between the new technology of the streaming service and the potential
      audience life context.
    </p>
    <ContentMedia kind="video" src="/casestudy/run/run" alt="Prototype of the run-pace-matched music player" width={640} height={370} />
  </ContentBlock>
</CaseStudyLayout>

<style>
  /* No aspect-ratio here: HeroImage's box already has definite heights
     (620/400/320) and .hero fills it; adding a ratio makes the width
     compute FROM the height and overflow the viewport on mobile. */
  .hero iframe {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
  }
</style>
